the big event was supposed to be  Saturday then it was pulled forward over  concern about far-right groups coming to  London this weekend  protesters rolled into town on bikes and  skateboards but reaching Hyde Park the  numbers were nothing on the scale of the  thousands last week the Prime Minister  and London's mayor asked people not to  protest because of the virus Boris  Johnson said the demonstrations had been  hijacked by extremists intent on  violence and said after it was  graffiti'd last week it was shameful  that the statue of Winston Churchill had  to be boarded up to protect it the  statue of of Winston Churchill who is a  national hero has had to be boarded up  for fear of violent attack and that to  me is both absurd and and we should look  sometimes at the positive stuff we've  got more young black and minority ethnic  kids going to university than ever  before more black kids doing the  toughest subjects in school doing better  than ever before looking at the  positives it's true the number of black  and ethnic minority students taking part  in further education has increased eight  percent in six years  but with school children this group  continues to have the highest temporary  exclusion rates and in business the  number of black and ethnic Directors in  the footsie 100 actually drops in 2019  we really are going backwards and the  people who are up there only about 15%  of them are English passport holders so  we are a net exporter of fame talent  while we're importing some of those  people in leadership positions in our  largest institution while this protest  was intent on being peaceful there are  still concerns about clashes at the  weekend we've certainly seen some people  who are talking about coming to London  for example to protect certain areas or  certain buildings that monuments and we  can anticipate that some of them  whatever their political persuasion our  intent some of them are intent on having  a confrontation with people from the  black lives matter  movement so my message is please just  stay away this weekend Winston Churchill  is not the only monument that's been  boarded up for protection there is a  concern that this focus on historic  figures and statues is detracting from  the more current message that the  protesters are trying to get across  everyone forgets the rule roots of evil  that we're dealing with right now we've  continued to deal with as a society and  as a black person which is institutional  racism today support the protest and  also make a change in the future  it's a political and policing challenge  the issues too important to stifle but  the risks of confrontation and violence  and the spread of the virus all too real  Jason Ferrell Sky News
 

